# GEMV y = A(512x512) * x(512), compute phase with accumulator readout.
# Mapping assumption:
# - LPDDR4 maps 512 matrix rows as 2 batches over 32 channels x 8 banks.
# - Each physical bank uses row 0 for output rows 0..255 and row 1 for output rows 256..511.
# - A 512-wide BF16 matrix row occupies 32 AiM 256b chunks.
# - The 512-element vector is written to the AiM Global Buffer.
# - channel_mask 0xffffffff targets all 32 channels.
# - MAC_ABK 32 expands to 32 column MAC commands across all banks.
# - A full 2KB physical row would be 64 chunks: 64 * 256b = 2KB.
#
# Note: On GDDR6_AiM_org, MAC_ABK would cover 32 channels x 16 banks = 512 banks in one batch.
AiM WR_GB 32 0 0xffffffff
W CFR 0 1
AiM WR_BIAS 64 0xffffffff
AiM MAC_ABK 32 0xffffffff 0
AiM RD_MAC 128 0xffffffff
AiM WR_BIAS 64 0xffffffff
AiM MAC_ABK 32 0xffffffff 1
AiM RD_MAC 128 0xffffffff
AiM ISR_EOC
